Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["LLM generated.", "GuideAbstract",ExpressionUUID->"f988fc30-4639-4a7d-85ac-4113510b0a44"],

Cell["\<\
Riemannian Infrageometry describes and distinguishes graphs as geometric \
substrates. In contrast, synthetic infrageometry asks only whether certain \
postulates are satisfied by the substrate so that its propositions about \
geometric objects hold. Riemann viewed space as an infinitesimal webbing of \
paths and, by imposing conditions on the infinitesimal length element, \
arrived at the quadratic metric tensor as the lowest-order data satisfying \
those conditions. This split continuous geometry into a manifold, which \
carries the topology and global analysis, and a Riemannian structure. This \
led people such as Gromov to ask about the moduli space of Riemannian \
structures on a fixed manifold, or, conversely, to derive topological \
quantities from Riemannian ones. In infrageometry, the discrete webbing of \
paths given by a graph is itself the geometric substrate, so no such split \
occurs. We relate infrageometry to continuous geometry through rescaled \
Gromov\[Dash]Hausdorff convergence, where the scaling is determined by the \
observer's scale. This yields a generalized definition of geometry: if a \
limit of rescaled graphs is a metric space arising from a Riemannian \
manifold, then that manifold is uniquely determined up to isomorphism.\
\>", "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A geodesic at observer scale ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "90c263a4-5345-4090-be3d-04cf8ca6674a"],
 " of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f5d33ca-5bb1-44f6-8427-7863db3cadd4"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraGeodesic"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraGeodesic", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["germ", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a3f8d64-c41d-4520-bd65-91966cf252d0"],
 ", is a family of walks of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9cc37e41-306d-43d8-a3ce-29e10686667b"],
 " that are shortest paths in every window of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c684c70b-d33e-42ab-a19b-227057803bbf"],
 " edges. A representative can be found with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["RandomInfraGeodesic"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraGeodesic", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", "\[Ellipsis]", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d603fce-112f-4762-8fc0-f6ac4f196d3a"],
 ", and the edge density of the corresponding multi-object with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["geodesic", "TI"], ",", " ", "\"\<EdgeDensity\>\""}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3abad706-7c01-444e-8ba4-ea4233440c0d"],
 "."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We can measure the volumes of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraBall"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraBall", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r0", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8f3f6130-4b7d-4131-a7c8-98eeab94000e"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "0"], "\[LessEqual]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26f89a42-2aba-4302-848e-ed017b7eb6e7"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraTube"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraTube", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["axis", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c037a3da-91ac-4062-b305-38017dde1653"],
 " for any ray or line through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65b30112-8b5f-4abe-98d6-3321621416a5"],
 " and any thickness ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e192ac63-f018-4dee-85f4-4910d1cad4d1"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraCone"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraCone", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["axis", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "84798885-572e-4665-ba02-284b1798d11c"],
 " for slope ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20c61348-1afc-43bd-a924-14837d1557e7"],
 ". Such measurements have asymptotic expansions in the continuous case and \
can be used to determine limiting curvature components. However, no sphere \
structure exists a priori on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraShell"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraShell", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3e045a77-46d9-43f4-ae70-d52227f15238"],
 ", so the limiting linear tensors can be compared only through histograms. \
We can also obtain the histogram of mutual distances between points, which \
constrains the limiting Riemannian manifold."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We have ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraTangentBundle"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraTangentBundle", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a95581c8-d815-4f8b-8540-59f6d21a3a89"],
 " which represents vectors at p by rays of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e7988ed0-c29e-4167-9a1c-9c030c2a1fae"],
 ", and these are compactly encoded as chains in the spray graph at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "87d6d7db-e274-40e6-9958-a201ddb33321"],
 ". We have an even simpler infra-bundle, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraDisplacementBundle"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraDisplacementBundle", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dfd8653-d155-4bee-a189-f12101f2face"],
 ", that keeps only the endpoints of rays. We have a minimal model of the \
Levi-Civita connection, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["FindInfraLeviCivitaConnection"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/\
FindInfraLeviCivitaConnection", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{"InfraDisplacementBundle", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a6bb88a-11e5-4af8-924b-ffde2a0c7830"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraParallelTransport"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraParallelTransport", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"InfraDisplacementBundle", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["walk", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b87280d6-a839-47ea-9b05-5726b141c135"],
 "."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We also have ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMetricTensor"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMetricTensor", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c974aa6-1ee7-4a11-9d3a-4bd603124554"],
 ", which computes shortest path projections of rays, displacement commutator \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["DisplacementCommutator"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/DisplacementCommutator", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["d1", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["d2", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d6892660-41de-442e-ae3c-1495c0605ac2"],
 ", and addition of displacements via midpoints with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["DisplacementSum"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/DisplacementSum", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["d1", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["d2", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e4637d6d-411e-4511-8f1f-324bfd5e9fbc"],
 ". These can be used to illustrate emergence of linearity."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

